From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/25] apklayer: aarch64-irelative

R_AARCH64_IRELATIVE (ifunc) relocations: the linker rejected them ("unknown reloc type 1032"). Chromium's libwebviewchromium.so has hundreds. As in bionic's linker, the resolver at base+addend is called with the hwcap (plus the _IFUNC_ARG_HWCAP bit) and an __ifunc_arg_t, and its result stored.

apklayer patch: step 9 of the former scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh (see docs/PATCHES.md), patch 0014 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 linker/linker.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/linker/linker.c b/linker/linker.c
index 1a40ed9..8592c2f 100644
--- a/linker/linker.c
+++ b/linker/linker.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #define LINKER_DEBUG_PRINTF(...)
 #endif
 
+#include <sys/auxv.h>
 #include <linux/auxvec.h>
 
 #include <assert.h>
@@ -1987,6 +1988,14 @@ static int apkenv_reloc_library(soinfo *si, REL_TYPE *rel, size_t count)
 			*((ElfW(Addr) *)reloc) = sym_addr + get_addend(rel);
 			break;
 #if defined(__aarch64__)
+		case R_AARCH64_IRELATIVE: { /* apklayer patch: IRELATIVE (ifunc), see scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh step 9 */
+			struct { unsigned long size, hwcap, hwcap2; } ifunc_arg = { sizeof(ifunc_arg), getauxval(AT_HWCAP), getauxval(AT_HWCAP2) };
+			ElfW(Addr) (*resolver)(unsigned long, void *) = (void *)(si->base + get_addend(rel));
+			COUNT_RELOC(RELOC_RELATIVE);
+			MARK(rel->r_offset);
+			*((ElfW(Addr) *)reloc) = resolver(ifunc_arg.hwcap | (1UL << 62), &ifunc_arg);
+			break;
+		}
 		case R_AARCH64_ABS64:
 			COUNT_RELOC(RELOC_ABSOLUTE);
 			MARK(rel->r_offset);
